From a82131c512921cc932cbe5d1986be44e1ccee09f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andras Lasso <lasso@queensu.ca>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 07:10:13 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] ENH: Render binary labelmap segmentations faster in 3D views

The colors of the segments are computed once per voxel of the grid (when
the labelmap or the colors change) instead of at every surface point of
every frame, which made rendering about three times faster.

ImageSampleDistance casts rays for every n-th pixel and scales the image
up to the viewport (color interpolated, depth, position and normal of the
frontmost surface for the render passes), as ImageSampleDistance of
vtkGPUVolumeRayCastMapper. It makes rendering faster while the camera is
moving, for example on mobile devices.

The previous render window is kept by weak pointer, and its context is
made current when its resources are released.
